{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_94142915#5_185127290","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is an NBC News article dedicated to racist bullying among Asian American youth, and its title/URL directly state the answer: 1 in 4, or 25%, of Asian American youths experience racist bullying.","learned":"A report/article on Asian American youth states that 25% (1 in 4) experience racist bullying."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2298","reason":"The racist-bullying query produced a strong grade-3 result; continue for additional exact percentage evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2298"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_94142915#1_185117954","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2298","rank":2,"snippet":"over the past year. The discrimination they detail primarily takes the form of verbal harassment, shunning and cyberbullying. The report was released Thursday by the Stop AAPI Hate Youth Campaign, a high school internship program at Stop AAPI Hate, a national center that collects reports of coronavirus discrimination against Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders. The study details the emotional toll of growing anti-Asian sentiment around the country. Nearly 8 of 10 respondents expressed anger over the epidemic of hate against Asians. The findings come from nearly 1,000 interviews of Asian American young adults conducted by a team of 87 Asian American high school <cover>students this summer. Full coverage of the coronavirus outbreak \"I think we hear this a lot, but the youth are the future,\" said Cassie Eng, a senior at the Urban School of San Francisco, who worked on the study. \"\" , \"start_char\": 826.000000 , \"title\": \"'You have Chinese virus!': 1 in 4 Asian American youths experience racist bullying, report says\" , \"url\": \"https://www.nbcnews.com/news/asian-america/25-percent-</cover>asian-american-youths-racist-bullying-n1240380\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"20/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_94142915#1_185117954","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of an NBC News article dedicated to racist bullying among Asian American youth; the title/URL directly state that 1 in 4, or 25%, of Asian American youths experience racist bullying, and the snippet describes the underlying Stop AAPI Hate youth report.","learned":"The Stop AAPI Hate Youth Campaign report, based on nearly 1,000 interviews of Asian American young adults, found that 25% (1 in 4) experienced racist bullying, primarily verbal harassment, shunning, and cyberbullying."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2298","reason":"The racist-bullying query is producing exact percentage evidence; continue to find additional documents or segments with race-based bullying percentages."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2298"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_94142915#2_185120132","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2298","rank":3,"snippet":"find our sense of self and our identity.\" The campaign, which is supported by the Jeremy Lin Foundation, grew out of the San Francisco Bay Area in the spring. During Asian Pacific American Heritage Month in May, students at Eng's school learned about the work Stop AAPI Hate had been doing and wanted to get more involved, so they reached out to the group to find out what they could do. Through their research, the <cover>students found that in addition to the racism they experienced themselves, Asian American youths have also been affected by the growing racism around the country, fueled by President Donald Trump's racist rhetoric, such as calling the coronavirus the \"China virus\" and \"kung flu.\" Nearly half of those interviewed expressed sadness or depression about the situation, and one-quarter said they were scared for themselves and their families.\" , \"start_char\": 1400.000000 , \"title\": \"'You have Chinese virus!': 1 in 4 Asian American youths experience racist bullying, report says\" , \"url\": \"https://www.nbcnews.com/news/asian-america/25-percent-</cover>asian-american-youths-racist-bullying-n1240380\" }"}}
