{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_465304437#1_952113224","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly provides an exact statistic for race/ethnicity/national origin as a reason for bullying: Davis & Nixon (2010) reported that about 16% of students reported this as a reason for bullying.","learned":"Davis & Nixon (2010) cited statistic: about 16% of students reported race, ethnicity, or national origin as a reason for bullying; looks was 55% and body shape 37%."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2328","reason":"This broader bullying-reason query produced a new direct percentage-bearing result, so continue to find additional documents with exact race/ethnicity bullying percentages."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2328"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_465304437#0_952111728","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2328","rank":2,"snippet":"can be the target of bullying. One out of 5 students report being a victim of bullying at some point (National Educational Statistics, 2016). Students who are bullied have increased school avoidance, decreases in grades, and difficulties with learning. These students often suffer from sleep difficulties, headaches and stomachaches, and mental health issues such as anxiety and depression. Students who are frequently <cover>bullied are two times more likely to have suicidal ideation or attempts (Gini & Espelage, 2014). Students who are bullies also have long-term issues such as academic problems, substance use, behavioral issues, and problems with the law. They are less likely to obtain meaningful employment and often struggle with independence and relationships as adults. There are many reasons why a student might be the victim of bullying. The research on race, ethnicity, and national origin are still not clear, but there are some studies that report this to be a reason </cover>for bullying.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"The Effects of Bullying - Rethink Education\" , \"url\": \"https://www.rethinked.com/blog/blog/2017/10/12/the-effects-of-bullying/\" }"}}
